invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_sign64_key_ok returns without wiping the product of the two
  primes. Under a key it admits that product is the modulus. Under a key
  with one bit of a prime changed it is not, and it and the modulus have
  the other prime as their common divisor. bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test runs
  the key test on a key with one bit of q changed, copies the stack below
  it and finds two limbs of the product that are not the modulus's.

--- old
    ct_wipe(q, sizeof q);
    ct_wipe(product, sizeof product);
--- new
    ct_wipe(q, sizeof q);
